WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:19.300
Sup yall? This week, we beastin through the darkness with "Les Miserables," by Victor Hugo.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:30.200
After 19 years of hard time in a French prison fo stealin bread to feed his fam, Jean Valjean all cashed out lookin fo help.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:36.540
Nobody in town showin him any love, til a righteous holy man named Myriel like, "come on in, padna!"

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:43.280
But, when da police catch Valjean tryna boost Myriel's silverware, Myriel jus' let it slide and tell the fuzz he

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:44.760
gave it to him as a gift.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:51.620
Myriel say, "look man, I just saved yo ass. You best stop all dat hood sh*t and become a better man, yo!"

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:57.240
After one last dick move — jackin some coin from a lil kid — Valjean break down and decide

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:03.060
he gotta put his bangin days behind him. He change his name to Monsieur Madeleine and move to a new town,

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:08.960
where he start stackin mad cheddar. Before you know it, brutha becomes the Goddamn mayor!

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:14.270
Meanwhile, this po girl, Fantine, be straight buggin — Number one, she desperate fo cash.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:18.200
And, number two — her man just left her with a love-child named Cosette,

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.740
and there ain't no way she gonna get work if word gets out about her.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:26.500
So, this shysti dude named Thenardier say Cosette can hide with him and his fam,

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:29.420
so long as Fantine throw em some ends erry month.

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:36.200
Fantine lands a gig grindin at Madeleine's factory, but gets da axe as soon as errybody find out bout Cosette.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:43.160
And with the Thenardiers greedy, lyin asses hittin her up fo mo cash, sh*t so raw for Fantine that she gotta sell

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:51.560
her hair, her teeth, and start turnin tricks on da streets. Plus, all this sh*t is literally killin her. Damn.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.280
One night, the local law-man, Javert, arrests Fantine,

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:01.060
but, Madeleine step in, tells Javert to hop off, and start to give Fantine a lil TLC.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:06.400
When Javert figure out Madeline's real identity, Javert cuff him right in front of Fantine.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.340
Girl wigs out so hard, she up and dies.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:14.680
By the way, Valjean's real identity only hit da streets cuz he wanted to save somebody's life.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:18.260
Thankfully, ain't no cell can keep dat boy, Valjean, down.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:24.540
Dude swings back to town to save Cosette from dem hater Thenardiers, who been treatin her like sh*t fo years.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:29.340
Valjean drop some fat stacks, buys her off em, and chunks deuces to Paris.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:35.420
Things aight in Paris fo a lil while, but when Javert hear that Valjean back in town, Val and Cosette

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:42.300
gotta pack their sh*t and lay low in a convent. Years later, a dude named Marius peep game at a dime and

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:49.680
immediately falls balls-deep in love! And, what do you know? It's Cosette, all grown up. Lookin good, girl!

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.460
Look what he said bout dis girl —

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:57.820
"The woman whom he now saw was a noble, beautiful creature, with all the most bewitching feminine outlines

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:04.400
at the precise moment when they are still combined with all the most charming graces of childhood — that pure

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:11.080
and fleeting moment that can only be translated by these two words: sweet fifteen." Ugh!

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:16.880
Marius try to holler at a girl, but Valjean moves they asses outta there before a brotha can get his mack on.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:22.580
Marius gets a tip about Cosette's new digs and they eventually meet and confess they love fo each other.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:27.300
'Cept, Valjean ain't down wit that. And, with all da political unrest goin down in the streets,

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.599
Valjean decides it's time fo them to roll out to England.

00:03:30.599 --> 00:03:36.479
Marius gets so tore up dat he ain't gonna be with his baby dip, that he decide he don't give a f**k no mo and

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:41.760
gonna join da revolution. When Valjean figure out dat Cosette and Marius are in love fo real,

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:47.180
he can't let loverboy get his ass murked, so he straps up and joins the fight, too.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:53.260
When da rebels find out that Javert a royalist snitch, they give Valjean the job of ghostin his ass.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:56.800
But, Valjean — bein a nice dude and all — just lets him walk away.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:03.160
Lata', Marius get pretty messed up and Valjean gotta carry his ass through some boo-boo sewers to get him help.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:09.480
Valjean runs in to Javert again, and Valjean finally like, "Aight, aight. You can arrest me.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:13.960
Just let me drop this dude off at his crib, and make one last stop at my pad."

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:17.820
Javert oblige a brotha, but start losin his sh*t when he realize he

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:21.900
compromising everything his life stood for, and straight ends it.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:28.220
Marius heals up and him and Cosette get hitched. S'all good, right? Nah. Not in this f**kin book.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:33.740
Valjean tells Marius about his crimin days, and Marius start givin Valjean the cold shoulder.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.560
Our boy gets da hint and stops droppin by.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:41.840
Dat little sh*t Marius got no idea it was Valjean that saved his ass in that sewer.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:48.000
With nothin left to live for, Valjean start wastin away, hops in bed, and doesn't ever leave.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:55.420
Lata', Marius conversatin wit Thenardier when brotha finally recognize dat da only reason he alive is cuz of Valjean.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:05:02.180
Plus, Valjean the only reason he wit Cosette now. Oh yeah — and Valjean left em mad bank.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:06.720
Feelin like a real assh*le, Marius and Cosette swing over to Valjean's spot and forgive him.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.820
Now, Valjean can die in peace.

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:21.020
Man, this book is straight relentless — gnarly prisons, po girls turnin tricks, disease wastin everybody!

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:26.900
V-hug gonna lay out da worst that life's got to offer, and he throws out his biggest beefs in the preface.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:32.480
"So long as there shall exist, by reason of law and custom, a social condemnation which,

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:40.380
in the midst of civilization, artificially creates a hell on earth, and complicates with human fatality a destiny that is divine;

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:45.780
so long as the three problems of the century — the degradation of man by the exploitation of his labor,

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:51.220
the ruin of woman by starvation, and the atrophy of childhood by physical and spiritual night —

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:56.480
are not solved; so long as, in certain regions, social asphyxia shall be possible;

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:02.780
in other words, and from a still broader point of view, so long as ignorance and misery remain on earth,

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:05.400
there should be a need for books such as this."

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:09.820
So, three big things he buckin — rich people takin advantage of da workin man,

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:14.760
women starving to death, and little kids drownin in a dark world dat ain't got no hope.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:19.320
In short, Hugo wagin war on a society that's f**kin over its peeps.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:22.980
In fact, that's one of Hugo's main jams in this big-ass book:

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:29.300
Society got da power to completely wreck somebody — and not only their body, but their soul, too.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:33.400
Whether it da big house dat turn Valjean into a stone-cold gangster,

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:39.280
or da poverty and shaming that make Fantine turn to a life of hookin — society burnin everybody.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:46.220
Like Valjean himself say, "The prison makes the convict. Make of this what you like. Before prison, I was a poor peasant,

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:54.000
unintelligent, a sort of idiot; prison changed me. I was stupid, I became wicked; I was a log, I became a firebrand."

00:06:54.000 --> 00:07:01.280
And, lemme tell you a lil somethin, man — society didn't break no regular erryday thug. Valjean is hella swole, man — fo real.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:08.500
On page 90, it even say he got the got da strength of four men. He still ain't got nuttin on deez guns. Don't hate.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:14.080
But no matter how jacked Valjean be, he still ain't got da muscle to flex with a broken system.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:19.700
Hugo's book ain't all bad, though. For Javert's ice-cold justice, there's Myriel's mercy.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:25.440
For Thenardier's greed, we see Valjean's willingness to give away everything — even his life.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:29.800
And, fo all the darkness that society can drop on a brotha, there's also light.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:35.380
We got da power to lift each other up and redeem erry brotha and sista with love and kindness.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:38.680
Valjean and Cosette reppin this idea perfectly:

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:43.060
"He loved, and he grew strong again. Alas, he was as frail as Cosette.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:47.960
He protected her, and she gave him strength. Thanks to him, she could walk upright in life;

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:53.980
thanks to her, he could persist in virtue. He was this child's support, and she was his prop and staff."

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:58.420
Valjean try to make this same point to a bunch of hoods while they gardening.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:04.340
"One day [Valjean] saw some peasants busily pulling out nettles; he looked at the heap of plants, uprooted, and

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:11.400
already wilted, and said, '…If we took a little time, the nettle would be useful; we neglect it, and it becomes harmful.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:16.940
Then we kill it. Men are so like the nettle!' After a short silence, he added, 'My friends, remember this:

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:22.020
There are no bad herbs, and no bad men; there are only bad cultivators."

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:29.300
As all my well-read ballas know, my number one motto is "Don't Judge a Book by its cover." Y'all know I'm all about that.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:33.680
But, lemme leave you with my number two motto, which "Les Mis" perfectly reppin:

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:37.960
Don't ever underestimate yo own power and how much of a difference you can make.

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:43.280
If you let anger, hatred, and injustice keep you down, ain't no tellin what kinda harm you can do.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:47.780
But, if you let love and light guide the way, then the world's dark side can't touch you.

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:51.200
You got da power to cultivate good in da world. Use it.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:56.080
Thanks for keepin it real with me, my well-read ballas. Sparky Sweets out! Peace!

